    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d447">

                <pb facs="0646" n="546" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg546"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.51 War Credits/682</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Greek Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Simopoulos</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-12-07">December 7, 1934</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am requested by the Secretary of the
                    Treasury to notify the Government of Greece that there was received on November
                    10, 1934, <pb facs="0647" n="547" xml:id="pg547"/> by the Federal Reserve Bank
                    of New York for credit in the account of the Treasurer of the United States, the
                    sum of $76,272 from the International Financial Committee, Athens, on behalf of
                    the Government of Greece representing a partial payment of interest due from
                    that Government on account of the 4% loan of 1929 made to the Greek Government
                    by the United States under the Funding Agreement of May 10, 1929.</p>
                <p>These funds were applied by the Treasury to the payment of 35% of the semi-annual
                    interest amounting to $217,920, due November 10, 1934, on the 4% loan of
                    1929.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed>R. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Walton Moore</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
